{
  "description": "Free composition (schema 9.19.0): cases shared by every reader of the contract. Data — `x-style.layout.composition`. Six tables. `nestingCases`: may `child` be a direct child of `parent` (the widget registry; since 9.19.0 a column, a row and a container accept their own type). `depthCases`: `chain` is a chain of containers under the screen root, `leaf` its innermost node; `depth` is the level of the leaf (the root is 0, its children 1); `valid` — whether the builder publishes the document (`max` levels below the root at most); the JSON Schema does not know the depth (`schema` is always true), and a reader draws any of these trees. `documentCases`: `children` are the children of the screen root of a two-screen document (`home` with these children and an empty `details`); `schema` — the verdict of the JSON Schema (Zod and ajv agree; the rows omit properties that have a default, as an author does — the JSON Schema describes the document after the defaults are filled in), `codes` — the codes of the validator (empty: publishable). `pressableCases`: is `node` a pressable container (`pressable`), a control that takes a press (`ownsPress`), a button on the finished screen (`acts`). `pressCases`: `tree` is a child of the screen root; a press lands on the box of the node `press` (the innermost node under the point); `receiver` is the node that takes the press — the innermost control on the way from the root (null: nobody); `runs` — the node whose action and analytics event are executed (null: nothing happens — the receiver is not a button, or `disabled` names it as a disabled button). No ancestor of the receiver gets anything. `instances` (optional): the tree is the template of a Repeater over this many records, the press lands in the instance number `instance` (from 0) and the action carries the record of THAT instance. `nameCases`: `tree` is a pressable container; `hasName` — whether it is heard without data (its `label`, or a text of a descendant that is not a control itself; since 9.19.0 the description `alt` of a picture or an icon is such a text — rows `9.19.0 …`, and `described` there lists the names of the images inside the card on a finished screen); `startsWith` — the accessible name of the button on a finished screen starts with this text (the label goes first); `heard` — texts the name must contain. The text of a control inside the container is not promised to be part of the name. Nor does the text of a control of the widget itself name the card — the header of an accordion, the titles of the tab strip (`pressable.semantics.ownControlTextWidgets`), — and the rule does not go into a list from data: its template is drawn once per record, so without data that text is not on the screen. What is silent is the class `x-accessibleName.silentCharacters`: a name is empty when nothing is left after the characters of the class are removed (rows `a description of …`).",
